SUMMARY:Feast of the Nativity of the Virgin\, Panagia Vrontiani monastery (Vourliotes)
LOCATION:Vourliotes\, Samos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Samos's oldest monastery (1566)\, above the mountain village of Vourliotes\, keeps its patronal feast with a hierarchical vespers on the evening of 7 September and liturgy and icon procession on the 8th\, presided by the Metropolitan of Samos. Pilgrims from the whole island come\; traditionally boiled meat with wheat is shared afterwards and the village square below fills for music. Narrow road\, so park in Vourliotes and walk the last stretch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#vourliotes-feast-of-the-nativity-of-the-virgin-panagia-vront
